    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8219" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνέμβᾰτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>inaccessible,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Eratosth.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				16.14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				1.3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. δρυμῶνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Babr.
					45.11
				</span></i>
			; of a river, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκαφέεσσιν ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.641
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>): metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ οὐσία τῶν πραγμάτων ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ocell.
					1.15
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βελέεσσιν ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					5.233.3
				</span></i>
			 (Paul. Sil.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>not to be trodden,</i> of a spot struck by a thunderbolt. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Pyrrh.</u>
				29
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>not going to</i> or <i>visiting,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				9.287
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Apollonid.
			</span></i>).</div>
